/-!
# Flat Artinian subalgebras essentially of finite type

Source: Stacks Project, Smoothing Ring Maps, Lemma 16.11.1 (Tag 07FG)
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-popescu-artinian-flat-subalgebras).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v w

namespace Algebra

/-- An Artinian local algebra in positive characteristic with finite first cotangent homology
of its residue field is a directed union of flat Artinian local subalgebras essentially of
finite type. The final clause spells out the colimit universal property for the inclusion
maps, using compatible families of algebra maps into any test algebra in `Type (max u v w)`.

Source: Stacks Project, Smoothing Ring Maps, Lemma 16.11.1 (Tag 07FG)
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-popescu-artinian-flat-subalgebras).

Proof (the twelve steps of the node):
1. By lem-weil-pbc-artinian-local-noetherian-nilpotent, the maximal ideal is finitely generated
   and has a vanishing power m^n. Choose generators lambda_i. The maps from k to Lambda and
   its residue field K are injective. A coefficient-field section sigma defines the map
   Psi_sigma from K[x_1,...,x_d] to Lambda sending x_i to lambda_i.
2. Induct on n to find sigma and a subfield F finitely generated over k for which the image
   of k lies in Psi_sigma(F[x]). For n = 1 take sigma to be the identity and F = k.
3. For n > 1 put I = m^(n-1). Then I^2 = mI = 0. Induction gives sigma' and F' modulo I.
   Lift sigma' using lem-weil-pbc-field-char-p-nilpotent-lifting. The truncated polynomial
   algebra F'[x]/(x)^n surjects onto the image A' modulo I with nilpotent kernel. The same
   lifting lemma lifts the induced map tau' from k to A' to a map tau into that algebra.
4. The difference theta = i - Psi_sigma composed with tau takes values in I and is a
   derivation, since I is square-zero and mI = 0. For any derivation D from K to I, sigma+D
   remains a ring section. Its effect on theta is to subtract D restricted to k: positive
   degree terms in tau contribute nothing to this difference because mI = 0.
5. Choose a basis dy_j of the differentials of k over F_p. The Jacobi-Zariski sequence
   (lem-weil-pbc-jacobi-zariski-homology-sequence) and finite dimensionality of H_1 give a
   finite set J_0 supporting the kernel of K tensor Omega_k to Omega_K. Therefore the dy_j
   outside J_0 have linearly independent images in Omega_K.
6. Extend those images to a basis and choose a K-linear map Omega_K to I agreeing with
   theta on them. Its associated derivation D makes theta-D restricted to k factor through
   the finite direct sum indexed by J_0. Write its finitely many values as f_j in I.
7. Express the f_j as sums of degree n-1 monomials in the lambda_i with coefficients in K.
   Adjoin these finitely many coefficients to F'. The new theta has values in Psi_sigma(F[x]),
   and so does Psi_sigma composed with tau. Their sum is i, proving the inductive claim.
8. Psi_sigma is surjective: Lambda equals its image plus m^r for every r, and m^n = 0.
   Its kernel is finitely generated by Hilbert's basis theorem
   (lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-algebra-noetherian). Enlarge F to F_0 containing all coefficients
   of these relations. For each finitely generated subfield F containing F_0, form A_F.
9. By lem-weil-pbc-tensor-quotient-base-change, the quotient B_F by these relations base
   changes to Lambda over K. By lem-weil-pbc-field-extension-base-change-faithfully-flat,
   B_F to Lambda is faithfully flat, hence injective by
   lem-weil-pbc-faithfully-flat-ideal-contraction. Its image A_F is thus isomorphic to B_F,
   and A_F to Lambda is flat.
10. The claim ensures A_F contains the image of k. It is a quotient of F[x]/(x)^n, hence
    finite dimensional over F and Artinian by lem-weil-pbc-finite-dim-algebra-artinian.
    Every element is sigma(c)+h with h in the nilpotent ideal generated by the lambda_i.
    It is a unit exactly when c is nonzero. This ideal is the maximal ideal of A_F, extends
    to m in Lambda, and the residue field of A_F is F.
11. A finitely generated field extension F/k is a localization of a finite type algebra.
    By lem-weil-pbc-artinian-local-essentially-finite-type-residue, A_F is essentially of
    finite type over k because its residue field F is.
12. Composita make these F and hence the A_F directed. Every element of Lambda has a
    polynomial representative; adjoining its finitely many coefficients to F_0 puts it in
    some A_F. The union is Lambda. Compatible maps on these subalgebras define a unique
    algebra map on this union, giving the filtered-colimit universal property. -/
theorem exists_directed_artinian_flat_subalgebras
    (k : Type u) [Field k] (Λ : Type v) [CommRing Λ] [Algebra k Λ]
    [IsArtinianRing Λ] [IsLocalRing Λ] (p : ℕ) [CharP k p] (hp : 0 < p)
    (hH : Module.Finite (IsLocalRing.ResidueField Λ)
      (H1Cotangent k (IsLocalRing.ResidueField Λ))) :
    ∃ S : Set (Subalgebra k Λ),
      DirectedOn (· ≤ ·) S ∧
      (∀ x : Λ, ∃ A ∈ S, x ∈ A) ∧
      (∀ A ∈ S, ∃ hA : IsLocalRing A,
        IsArtinianRing A ∧ RingHom.Flat A.val.toRingHom ∧
        Ideal.map A.val.toRingHom (@IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A _ hA) =
          IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Λ ∧ EssFiniteType k A) ∧
      (∀ (T : Type (max u v w)) [CommRing T] [Algebra k T]
        (f : ∀ A : S, A.1 →ₐ[k] T),
        (∀ (A B : S) (h : A.1 ≤ B.1),
          (f B).comp (Subalgebra.inclusion h) = f A) →
        ∃! g : Λ →ₐ[k] T, ∀ A : S, g.comp A.1.val = f A) := by
  sorry

end Algebra
